  "enhanced_information": "Becker muscular dystrophy (BMD) is primarily an alteration of the skeletal muscle, caused by mutations in the dystrophin gene, which is crucial for maintaining muscle integrity. This genetic disorder leads to progressive muscle weakness and degeneration, predominantly affecting males due to its X-linked recessive inheritance pattern. The evidence paths confirm that BMD is associated with muscular atrophy and muscle necrosis linked to dystrophin deficiency, further supporting the consensus that the condition primarily impacts skeletal muscle function."
